.TH SDL_HINT_QUIT_ON_LAST_WINDOW_CLOSE 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_QUIT_ON_LAST_WINDOW_CLOSE \- A variable that decides whether to send
.BR SDL_EVENT_QUIT
when closing the last window.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_QUIT_ON_LAST_WINDOW_CLOSE \(dqSDL_QUIT_ON_LAST_WINDOW_CLOSE\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: SDL will not send an
.BR SDL_EVENT_QUIT
event when the last window is requesting to close\[char46] Note that in this case, there are still other legitimate reasons one might get an
.BR SDL_EVENT_QUIT
event: choosing \(dqQuit\(dq from the macOS menu bar, sending a SIGINT (ctrl-c) on Unix, etc\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: SDL will send a quit event when the last window is requesting to close\[char46] (default)
.PP
If there is at least one active system tray icon,
.BR SDL_EVENT_QUIT
will instead be sent when both the last window will be closed and the last tray icon will be destroyed\[char46]
.PP
This hint can be set anytime\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

